 "steps": [
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Snap off each head, split the belly with your thumbnail and pull out the dark guts.</li><li>Both make the dashi bitter.</li><li>Small niboshi can go in whole; for the bigger ones, this step matters.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-1",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Clean the niboshi",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Snap off each head.",
      "src": "illustrations/niboshi-bonito-dashi/1-how1.webp"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Split the belly with your thumbnail and pull out the dark guts — they make the dashi bitter.",
      "src": "illustrations/niboshi-bonito-dashi/1-how2.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/niboshi-bonito-dashi/1.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 1,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~8 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~8 min</span>",
   "title": "Clean the niboshi",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"20\">20 g</span>",
     "name_html": "Niboshi (larger dried anchovies)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Put the cleaned niboshi (and the kombu, if using) in a saucepan with <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"l\" data-a=\"1\" data-s=\"0\">1 litre</span> of cold water.</li><li>Soak at least 30 minutes, or overnight in the fridge.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-2",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Soak",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [],
    "illustration": "illustrations/niboshi-bonito-dashi/2.webp",
    "photo": null,
    "result": null,
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 2,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "30 min+",
   "time_html": "<span>30 min+</span>",
   "title": "Soak",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"l\" data-a=\"1\">1 l</span>",
     "name_html": "Water"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"5\" data-b=\"10\">5–10 g</span>",
     "name_html": "Kombu"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Bring up to temperature slowly over medium-low heat.</li><li>If you used kombu, lift it out as soon as small bubbles appear — before it boils.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "medium-low",
    "label_html": "<span>medium-low</span>",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-3",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Heat slowly, kombu out",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "When small bubbles appear, lift the kombu out — before it boils.",
      "src": "illustrations/niboshi-bonito-dashi/3-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/niboshi-bonito-dashi/3.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 3,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~10 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~10 min</span>",
   "title": "Heat slowly, kombu out",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<p>Let the niboshi simmer gently for 5–10 minutes, skimming off any foam.</p>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "low",
    "label_html": "<span>low</span>",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-4",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Simmer and skim",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Skim off any foam as it simmers.",
      "src": "illustrations/niboshi-bonito-dashi/4-how1.webp"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/niboshi-bonito-dashi/4.webp",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 4,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "5–10 min",
   "time_html": "<span>5–10 min</span>",
   "title": "Simmer and skim",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<p>Turn off the heat, scatter in the katsuobushi and leave it for about 2 minutes, until the flakes sink.</p>",
